      "id": "c2a4ba4f-ae37-4bda-9680-eca12bea4117",
      "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
      "data": {
        "body": "Three students present statements about how to find the speed \\(v_0\\) at which the block is launched into the air at the top of the spring. Which is correct?\n\n\\textbf{Beth:} You choose the block as the system and everything else in the surroundings and your equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}Mv_0^2-0\\right)=-Mg(L_0-L)\\sin\\theta+\\frac{1}{2}k_s(L_0-L)^2-\\mu_kMg(L_0-L)\\cos\\theta\n\\]\n\n\\textbf{Amy:} You choose the block and spring as the system and everything else in the surroundings and your equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}Mv_0^2-0\\right)+\\left(0-\\frac{1}{2}k_s(L_0-L)^2\\right)=-Mg(L_0-L)\\sin\\theta-\\mu_kMg(L_0-L)\\cos\\theta\n\\]\n\n\\textbf{Cathy:} You choose the block, spring, and Earth in the system, and ramp in the surroundings, then your equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}Mv_0^2-0\\right)+\\left(0-Mg(L_0-L)\\sin\\theta\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}k_s(L_0-L)^2-\\mu_kMg(L_0-L)\\cos\\theta\n\\]",
        "solution": [
          1
        ],
        "answerChoices": [
          {
            "id": "c94f01b9-ec52-49aa-8954-0258c2c2c2d8",
            "index": 0,
            "body": "Amy and Cathy are correct, Beth is wrong",
